---
id: org.dxos.plugin.presenter
name: PresenterPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

A presentation plugin for DXOS Composer. A Presentation is an ordered deck of sections, each an owned markdown slide or a link to any workspace object, shown in the navtree as a folder of slides and presented with fullscreen mode and keyboard navigation. A markdown document can still be previewed as a deck through its Presenter companion. Slides are written in a strict Slidev subset (layouts, slots, click steps, notes) with DXOS extensions (video backgrounds, embedded object surfaces).

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`       |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`       |
| `scenario`  | `org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0`   |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`  |
| `op`        | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.1`         |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`       |
| `step`      | `org.dxos.mdl.step@1.0`       |
| `decision`  | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0`   |

## Types

```mdl
type Presentation
  desc: |
    An ordered deck of slides. Typename `org.dxos.type.presentation@0.2.0`. Each slide is a `Slide` object owned
    by the presentation. It is tagged as a collection item, so it is filed into the space's Collections. Its
    navtree node lists `slides`; deleting a slide deletes its `Slide` (and the slide's owned `Text`), while a
    linked object it shows is only unlinked. Deleting the Presentation deletes its slides; linked objects stay.
    Version 0.1.0 held `sections: Ref<Obj>[]` directly; its migration wraps each section in a `Slide`.
    A plugin-projects showcase is a Presentation (see CreateShowcase); a `Showcase` 0.1.0 migrates into one in
    place, its markdown the first slide and each artifact a linked slide, so its `Demonstrates` edges still hold.
  fields:
    name?: string
    description?: string
    slides: Ref<Slide>[]        # slide order
    theme?: SlideTheme.Settings # deck theme; overrides the first slide's `theme:` headmatter
```

```mdl
type Slide
  desc: |
    One slide of a Presentation, owned by it. Typename `org.dxos.type.slide@0.1.0`. Its `content` is either an
    owned markdown `Text` (parented to the Slide, written in the Slidev subset of F-6) or a link to any other
    ECHO object, rendered through its `role=slide` surface. The fields hold what applies to any content, so a
    linked object can be hidden, annotated and given an image as a markdown slide can; `layout` and
    `background` stay in a markdown slide's frontmatter. A slide opened from the navtree or the grid opens the
    `Slide`, so the assistant beside it has the slide as its context.
  fields:
    content: Ref<Obj>           # owned Text or a linked object
    title?: string              # overrides the label read from the content's first heading
    hidden?: boolean            # left out when presenting; replaces frontmatter `hide:`
    notes?: Ref<Text>           # speaker notes for any slide
    image?: Ref<MediaArtifact>  # the image a layout places (cover and image layouts), from plugin-studio
    duration?: number           # desired length in seconds, shown against the time on the slide while presenting
    takes?: Ref<Variant>[]      # recorded voice-over takes (plugin-recorder), owned by the slide
    mainTake?: Ref<Variant>     # the take that voices the slide
```

```mdl
type SlideViewState
  desc: |
    Per-user, per-deck view state (`presenter-slide`, local backend) in `@dxos/react-ui-attention`,
    keyed by the Presentation's (or previewed document's) URI. Never syncs to collaborators.
  fields:
    index: number               # zero-based index of the slide this user is viewing; clamped to the deck on read
```

```mdl
type PresenterSettings
  desc: |
    The plugin's settings (`PresenterSettings.Settings`, persisted per device).
  fields:
    notes?: off | subtitles | window   # where speaker notes show while presenting; default off
```

```mdl
type SlideTheme
  desc: |
    A deck's theme settings (`SlideTheme.Settings`): a built-in theme name and optional overrides. Applied as
    `--slide-*` CSS variables on each slide; linked object slides are painted with the same variables.
  fields:
    name?: default | light | dark | serif
    accent?: string             # plain CSS color
    background?: string         # plain CSS color
    foreground?: string         # plain CSS color
    font?: string               # font-family list for body and headings
```

```mdl
type SlideSource
  literals: text | object | markdown | pending
  desc: |
    One slide of a deck: `text` is an owned Text rendered as markdown; `object` is any linked object (a
    Markdown.Document included) rendered through the slide surface fallback; `markdown` is one `---`-separated
    slide of a previewed document (its id is positional); `pending` is a section whose
    target has not loaded yet. A section whose target was deleted yields no slide.
```

## Components

```mdl
component Deck
  desc: |
    A composite (`Deck.Root`, headless, holding the state and keys; `Deck.Content`, the focus scope that handles keys
    and prints; `Deck.Viewport`, the current slide; `Deck.Grid`, every slide as a thumbnail; `Deck.Pager`,
    `Deck.PageNumber` and `Deck.PlayButton`), composed by its containers into a Panel.
    Paged slide deck. Inline it shows the pager centered in a status bar below the slide; in fullscreen an overlay pager that auto-hides when idle
    and wakes on pointer movement. Keys are scoped to the deck's focus scope, never `window`: left and right
    step, Shift+left and Shift+right (or Home and End) jump to first and last, `f` toggles fullscreen,
    Escape exits fullscreen. Space and right advance a click step, else the slide; left retreats a click step,
    else lands on the previous slide fully revealed. Click steps are ephemeral and reset on slide change; Space
    does not act on a focused button or link. While the focused (or fullscreen) deck prints, it renders every
    slide into a print-only container, one 16:9 page each with every click step shown, and drops the rest of the
    app from the printout.
  props:
    slides: SlideSource[]       # Deck.Root
    index: number               # Deck.Root
    fullscreen: boolean         # Deck.Root
    theme?: SlideTheme          # Deck.Root; without a name, the first slide's `theme:` headmatter applies
  actions:
    onIndexChange(index: number)              # Deck.Root
    onFullscreenChange(fullscreen: boolean)   # Deck.Root
    onAddSlide()                              # Deck.Viewport; offered when the deck is empty
    onMove(from: number, to: number)          # Deck.Grid; enables dragging thumbnails
  layout: |
    ┌─────────────────────────────┐
    │ [toolbar]              [⛶] │  ← hidden in fullscreen
    ├─────────────────────────────┤
    │                             │
    │   Deck.Viewport (slide N)   │
    │   (overlay pager, idle)     │
    ├─────────────────────────────┤
    │      ◀◀ ◀  3 / 12  ▶ ▶▶     │  ← status bar; hidden in fullscreen and in the grid view
    └─────────────────────────────┘
  grid: |
    ┌─────────────────────────────┐
    │ [toolbar]              [⛶] │
    ├─────────────────────────────┤
    │ ┌────┐ ┌────┐ ┌────┐ ┌────┐ │  ← Deck.Grid: thumbnails, current one outlined;
    │ │ 1  │ │ 2  │ │[3] │ │ 4  │ │    scrolls vertically; columns follow the width
    │ └────┘ └────┘ └────┘ └────┘ │
    │ ┌────┐                      │
    │ │ 5  │                      │
    │ └────┘                      │
    └─────────────────────────────┘
```

```mdl
component PresentationArticle
  desc: |
    A Presentation's article is a grid of its slides (`Deck.Grid`); presenting shows one slide at a time (`Deck.Viewport`).
    Fullscreen is read per object (is this Presentation on the
    fullscreen plank) and toggles in place on the Presentation's own plank; the current slide is per-viewer
    view state. The toolbar adds slides and links objects through SectionPicker.
  props:
    subject: Presentation
    attendableId?: string
```

```mdl
component SlideEditorArticle
  desc: |
    Article for an owned slide, opened by clicking the slide's child node in the navtree. A toolbar (formatting,
    slide tools, view controls) sits above the markdown editor; the rendered slide shows below it in a vertical
    split, or in the plank's companion. Cursor and preview stay in sync both ways.
  props:
    subject: Text
```

```mdl
component SectionPicker
  desc: |
    Toolbar picker ("Add to presentation") over the space's objects that links the chosen object into the
    presentation as a section. It queries the space only while open; an unnamed object is listed as
    "Untitled <type>".
  props:
    presentation: Presentation
```

```mdl
component Slide
  desc: |
    A composite: `Slide.Root` (headless) holds one SlideSource and its options; `Slide.Frame` is a fixed 16:9
    logical canvas scaled to its container (inset in a solid void with `inset`, unscaled for print), so every slide
    contributor designs for one size; `Slide.Content` draws the source. Text sources render markdown through
    MarkdownSlide; markdown sources (the preview companion's raw slides) do the same; pending sources show a
    loading slide; object sources render through the AppSurface.Slide surface, falling back to a title slide while
    no surface matches, and request gated slide surfaces on demand. It supplies MarkdownSlide's embedded surfaces
    from the database of the slide's owner.
  props:
    source: SlideSource         # Slide.Root
    step?: number               # Slide.Root
    inset?: boolean             # Slide.Frame
```

```mdl
component MarkdownSlide
  desc: |
    Renders one slide of the Slidev markdown subset on the 2560x1440 canvas: per-slide frontmatter
    (`layout`, `image`, `background`, `class`, `backgroundVideo`, `backgroundOpacity`, `backgroundPosition`,
    `bleed`, and `theme` on the first slide; `title` is parsed and reserved, not rendered),
    `::default::` / `::left::` / `::middle::` / `::right::` / `::bottom-left::` / `::bottom-right::` slots,
    `<v-click>`, `<v-clicks>` (`depth`, `every`) and `<v-after>` click steps, highlighted code blocks with
    static line ranges, and notes. All other raw HTML is escaped, never rendered. Elements with a later click
    step stay laid out but invisible. `class:` accepts only Tailwind utilities already generated.
  props:
    content: string
    step?: number               # undefined reveals everything
    renderSurface?: (uri, role) => ReactNode
```

```mdl
component SlideLayouts
  desc: |
    The layouts a slide's `layout` names: default, cover, center, section, intro, end, fact, statement, quote,
    two-cols, two-cols-header, three-cols, two-by-two, image, image-left, image-right, full, none. An unknown
    name renders with default and is reported as a validation issue. `bleed: left | right` takes the outer column
    of `two-cols` or `three-cols` to the slide's edges.
  props:
    slots: { default, left, middle, right, bottom-left, bottom-right }
    frontmatter: SlideFrontmatter
```

```mdl
component SlideBackground
  desc: |
    The slide's background: a colour, an `image`, or a looping, muted, autoplaying `backgroundVideo`, with
    `backgroundOpacity` and `backgroundPosition`. In the `image` layout a theme scrim sits between the
    picture and any slide content so text over a photo stays legible; other layouts draw no scrim.
  props:
    frontmatter: SlideFrontmatter
    layout: string
```

```mdl
component EmbeddedSurface
  desc: |
    Renders the object a slide's `<Surface ref="echo:///<id>" role="slide|section|card" />` names, through
    ObjectSurface (fallback `slide`, `section`, `card`, then a title slide). A malformed, missing or deleted
    ref settles on a "Missing object" placeholder, never a spinner left running; a space-qualified ref
    resolves only while that space is open in the client. A ref to a `Text` (such as another deck's owned
    slide) renders that markdown as a scaled slide, whose own `<Surface>`s stay placeholders. An embed of an
    object that already encloses it (the slide's own subject, or a cycle), or one nested more than 3 levels
    deep, renders an "Embedded in itself" placeholder instead.
  props:
    uri: string
    role: slide | section | card
    db: Database
```

```mdl
component DocumentArticle
  desc: |
    Presenter companion of a Markdown document: the shared Deck over the document content, split into slides
    on horizontal `---` separators outside fenced code, honouring leading headmatter and per-slide frontmatter
    (markdown sources). Vertical slides are not configured. Nothing is persisted. Fullscreen is read
    per object from the deck's fullscreen plank (is this document presented), not from the global layout mode.
  props:
    document: Markdown.Document
  actions:
    exit()                      # exits fullscreen for this document
```

```mdl
component SlideArticle
  desc: |
    The AppSurface.Slide surface for Markdown.Document objects: renders the document as a slide, without a
    frame (Slide.Frame owns it).
  props:
    document: Markdown.Document
```

```mdl
component SpeakerNotes
  desc: |
    A composite: `SpeakerNotes.Subtitles` shows the current slide's notes over the bottom of a presented slide;
    `SpeakerNotes.Prompter` is the speaker's view: the slide's notes large (one line per bullet or sentence), its
    position, the time on the slide against its desired length (flagged when over), and the next slide's notes.
  props:
    lines: string[]             # Subtitles, Prompter
    title?: string              # Prompter
    next?: { title?, lines }    # Prompter
    index: number               # Prompter
    count: number               # Prompter
    elapsed: number             # Prompter; seconds on the slide
    duration?: number           # Prompter; the slide's desired length
```

```mdl
component PresentedOverlay
  desc: |
    Drawn over a presented Presentation (inside `Deck.Viewport`): the speaker notes as the `notes` setting asks —
    subtitles, or a second browser window (a portal, so it shares the app's state; keys pressed there move the deck;
    a refused popup offers a button to open it) — the `PresenterSurface.Overlay` slot, and the
    `PresentationEventHandler` callbacks: start on mount, stop on unmount, and every slide or click-step change.
  props:
    presentation: Presentation
```

Extension points: `PresenterSurface.Toolbar` (data `{ subject: Presentation }`) adds items to a Presentation's
toolbar before the play button; `PresenterSurface.Overlay` draws over the presented deck; the
`PresentationEventHandler` capability (`onStart`, `onSlide({ presentation, slide?, id, title?, index, step })`,
`onStop`) follows a presentation. Another plugin (the recorder) uses them; presenter depends on none of them.

## Operations

```mdl
op TogglePresentation
  key: org.dxos.operation.presenter.setPresenting
  desc: |
    Enters or exits presentation for a Markdown document or Presentation by toggling the deck's
    fullscreen overlay (EphemeralDeckState.fullscreen). A Markdown document presents through its presenter
    companion node; a Presentation presents fullscreen on its own plank, since its article is the deck.
    The overlay is independent of what is open, so neither direction navigates: the URL and the
    open planks are unchanged.
  input:
    object: Markdown.Document | Presentation
    state: boolean              # on or off; callers that flip read the current state first
  output: void
  effects: [deck:fullscreen]
  requires: [DeckCapabilities.EphemeralState, DeckOperation.Adjust]
  note: |
    For a document the path is `<objectPath>/~presenter`; for a Presentation it is the plank's own path.
    Keyboard shortcut: Shift+Cmd+P (macOS), Shift+Alt+P (Windows/Linux).
```

```mdl
op CreateShowcase
  key: org.dxos.operation.projects.createShowcase
  desc: |
    Declared by plugin-projects, whose project skill offers it, and implemented here. Makes a Presentation whose
    first slide is an owned markdown `Text` holding `content` (`# <name>` when it is blank) and whose further
    slides each link one of `artifacts` in order, such as an image or video `File`, a diagram or a `PullRequest`;
    each renders through the slide surface fallback. When `content` is a whole deck that F-6.7's rule splits into
    more than one slide, each part becomes an owned slide in order, keeping its frontmatter and notes, before the
    artifact slides. A `Demonstrates` relation goes from the deck to each target. Every target and artifact is
    loaded before anything is written.
  input:
    name: string
    content: string             # markdown for the first slide, or a whole deck
    targets: Ref<Obj>[]         # the features and tasks it demonstrates
    artifacts?: Ref<Obj>[]      # one linked slide each
  output:
    showcase: Presentation
  effects: [echo:write]
  requires: [Database.Service]
```

```mdl
op GenerateSlideImage
  key: org.dxos.operation.presenter.generateSlideImage
  desc: |
    Generates an image for a slide from a prompt with plugin-studio's `StudioOperation.Generate` (image kind,
    the space's configured provider), stores it as a `MediaArtifact`, and sets it as the slide's `image`. A
    markdown slide whose layout places no image is switched to `layout: image` (or keeps an `image-left` /
    `image-right` / `cover` layout it already has).
  input:
    slide: Ref<Slide>
    prompt: string
  output:
    artifact: Ref<MediaArtifact>
  effects: [echo:write]
  requires: [Database.Service, Operation.Service]
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Presentation Mode

  req F-1.1: Every Markdown document in the workspace has a companion "Presenter" node in the app graph.
  req F-1.2:
    when: user activates TogglePresentation on a document
    then: the presenter companion fills the screen in the deck's fullscreen overlay, without the companion tab strip, and the URL does not change
  req F-1.3:
    when: user presses Shift+Cmd+P (macOS) or Shift+Alt+P (Windows)
    then: TogglePresentation is invoked for the focused object
  req F-1.4:
    when: user activates TogglePresentation on a Presentation
    then: the Presentation's own plank fills the screen in the fullscreen overlay and the URL does not change
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Document Preview

  req F-2.1:
    when: DocumentArticle mounts with a Markdown.Document
    then: the Deck renders the document content as slides
  req F-2.2: Slides are separated by horizontal `---`; vertical slides are not configured.
  req F-2.3:
    when: user presses Escape or the exit action is triggered
    then: fullscreen exits for that document, leaving it and its companion as they were
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Presentation Object

  req F-3.1: A Presentation is created from the space's create-object menu, is filed into the space's Collections, and holds an ordered `sections` array.
  req F-3.2: One section is exactly one slide; `---` inside a section is a horizontal rule, not a slide break.
  req F-3.3: A section is an owned markdown Text (parented to the presentation) or a link to any object.
  req F-3.4:
    when: user adds a slide from the toolbar
    then: a new owned Text section is appended
  req F-3.5:
    when: user links an object through SectionPicker
    then: the object becomes a section and keeps its own parent
  req F-3.6:
    when: an owned slide is deleted with the space's Delete
    then: it leaves the deck and the navtree, and the delete can be undone
  req F-3.7:
    when: a linked section is removed from the presentation
    then: only the link is removed; the object remains
  req F-3.8: Presentation deletion does not cascade to linked objects.
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Presentation Deck

  req F-4.1:
    when: PresentationArticle mounts
    then: the slide at the viewer's stored index is shown, clamped to the deck
  req F-4.2: The pager shows the current slide and total count; an empty deck shows none.
  req F-4.3: Keys bind to the deck's focus scope, never `window`.
  req F-4.4:
    when: user presses `f`
    then: the deck toggles fullscreen in place
  req F-4.5:
    when: the deck is fullscreen and the pointer is idle
    then: the overlay pager hides, and shows again on pointer movement
  req F-4.6:
    when: user presses Escape in fullscreen
    then: the deck exits fullscreen
  req F-4.7: The current slide index is per-user view state, kept across navigation and reloads, and never shared with collaborators.
  req F-4.8: Only an attended deck takes focus on mount.
  req F-4.9: A linked object with no slide surface renders as a title slide rather than failing.
  req F-4.10: A section whose target was deleted is omitted from the deck; one whose target has not loaded shows a pending slide.
  req F-4.11: Inline, a Presentation shows every slide as a fully revealed thumbnail in a vertically scrolling grid with no pager; the current slide is selected, and arrow keys or a click move it.
  req F-4.12:
    when: user drags a thumbnail before or after another
    then: the section moves there, and the moved slide stays current
  req F-4.13:
    when: user double-clicks a thumbnail
    then: the deck presents fullscreen from that slide
```

```mdl
feat F-6: Markdown Slides

  req F-6.1: A slide is written in a strict Slidev subset: per-slide frontmatter `layout`, `image`, `background`, `class`, `title` (and the DXOS keys of F-8.1 and F-8.5 and the `theme` headmatter of F-6.8); slots `::left::`, `::right::`, `::default::`, and for the DXOS layouts `three-cols` and `two-by-two` also `::middle::`, `::bottom-left::` and `::bottom-right::`; notes as the slide's last HTML comment.
  req F-6.2: The layouts are default, cover, center, section, intro, end, fact, statement, quote, two-cols, two-cols-header, three-cols, two-by-two, image, image-left, image-right, full and none.
  req F-6.3:
    when: a slide names an unknown layout
    then: it renders with default, no error is shown, and a validation issue is reported
  req F-6.4:
    when: a slide's frontmatter YAML is malformed
    then: the body still renders, the frontmatter is ignored and a validation issue is reported
  req F-6.5: Raw HTML other than `v-click`, `v-clicks`, `v-after`, `Surface` and `br` is escaped, never rendered or executed; URLs with unsafe schemes are not followed.
  req F-6.6: A fenced code block renders highlighted; a `{2,4-5}` meta marks the lines that stay emphasised, and Slidev's `{lines:true}` option numbers the lines.
  req F-6.7: In the preview companion `---` splits slides except inside a fenced code block, and a leading frontmatter block is slide metadata.
  req F-6.8: A deck has one theme, `default`, `light`, `dark` or `serif`, named by the first slide's `theme:` headmatter; `default` follows the app's light/dark mode and `light`/`dark` force one, code highlighting included.
  req F-6.9: A Presentation's `theme` setting names the theme and may override its accent, background and text colors, its text font (`mono`, `sans`, `rounded`, `serif`, `display`, `space-grotesk`, `mali`, `geist`, `orbitron`, `unbounded`, `opendyslexic`, `lxgw-wenkai`) and its code font (`jetbrains`, `fira`, `plex`, `system`); it wins over headmatter, and linked object slides are painted with it too.
  req F-6.10:
    when: a slide names an unknown theme, or an override is not a plain color or font list
    then: the default theme or value applies and, for an unknown name, a validation issue is reported
```

```mdl
feat F-7: Click Steps

  req F-7.1: `<v-click>`, `<v-clicks>` (`depth`, `every`) and `<v-after>` reveal their content one click at a time; a hidden element keeps its layout.
  req F-7.2:
    when: user presses Space or right with steps remaining
    then: the next step reveals, and only after the last step does the deck advance
  req F-7.3:
    when: user presses left with steps revealed
    then: the last step hides; at step 0 the previous slide shows fully revealed
  req F-7.4: Click steps reset on any slide change and are never persisted; only the slide index is view state.
  req F-7.5: Space on a focused button or link activates it and does not advance.
```

```mdl
feat F-8: Backgrounds and Embedded Surfaces

  req F-8.1: Frontmatter `backgroundVideo` plays as a looping, muted, autoplaying background, with `backgroundOpacity` and `backgroundPosition`.
  req F-8.2:
    when: a slide contains `<Surface ref="echo:///<id>" role="slide|section|card" />` in any slot
    then: the referenced object renders there through its slide surface, falling back to section, card and a title slide
  req F-8.3:
    when: the ref is malformed, never existed, or its target is deleted
    then: a "Missing object" placeholder shows in its place, with no spinner left
  req F-8.4: An image whose URL is an object URI (`![label](echo:///<id>)`) embeds that object as `<Surface ref>` with the `slide` role; alone in its paragraph it fills its slot, and the label is ignored.
  req F-8.5: Frontmatter `bleed: left` or `bleed: right` takes the outer column of a `two-cols` or `three-cols` slide to the slide's edges on that side, top and bottom, with no padding, for an embedded object to fill.
```

```mdl
feat F-9: Printing

  req F-9.1:
    when: the focused or fullscreen deck is printed
    then: every slide of the deck prints, one per 16:9 page at full size, with every click step shown and the app chrome, overlay and other decks left out
  req F-9.2: Print rules apply only while a deck is printing, so printing anything else in the app is unaffected.
```

```mdl
feat F-10: Slide Editor

  req F-10.1: The slide editor has a toolbar with markdown formatting, slide tools (layout, click step, column break, object, background, notes) and view controls (preview mode, previous/next slide, present from here).
  req F-10.2: Picking a layout writes the slide's `layout:` frontmatter, keeping its other keys; each toolbar edit is one undo step.
  req F-10.3: The preview shows below the editor in a resizable vertical split, or in the plank's companion; the mode and split position are kept per user.
  req F-10.4:
    when: the cursor is inside a `<v-click>` or `<v-clicks>` group
    then: the preview reveals up to that group's step, and in a slotted layout the cursor's slot is outlined
  req F-10.5:
    when: user clicks an element in the preview
    then: the editor's caret moves to the start of that element's source (no range is selected) and scrolls into view
  req F-10.6: "Present from here" opens the deck fullscreen at this slide.
```

```mdl
feat F-5: Navtree Folder

  req F-5.1: A Presentation node lists its sections as children.
  req F-5.2: An owned slide is labelled by its name, else its first markdown heading, else "Slide N".
  req F-5.3:
    when: user drags a child to a new position
    then: `sections` is reordered to match
  req F-5.4:
    when: user clicks a slide child
    then: the slide's own article opens (SlideEditorArticle for an owned slide)
  req F-5.5: An owned slide offers no remove action, only the space's Delete; a linked section's remove action is labelled "Remove from presentation".
  req F-5.6: The children are the deck's slides in deck order, so a deleted section leaves both.
```

```mdl
feat F-11: Slides as Objects

  req F-11.1: A Presentation's slides are `Slide` objects, each holding its content (an owned Text or a linked object) and the slide's own metadata (title, hidden, notes, image).
  req F-11.2: A Presentation has an optional description.
  req F-11.3: Opening a slide opens its `Slide`; the assistant companion beside it has the Slide, its content and its presentation as context, with the presenter skill enabled.
  req F-11.4:
    when: the assistant is asked for an image on the slide it is beside
    then: it calls `GenerateSlideImage`, and the slide shows the generated image in its layout
  req F-11.5: An image is held as a ref to a plugin-studio `MediaArtifact`, which the slide background resolves to its image.
  req F-11.6: Presentations of version 0.1.0 migrate in place: each section becomes a `Slide`, and a markdown slide's `hide: true` becomes `hidden`.
```

```mdl
feat F-12: Speaker Notes

  req F-12.1: A slide's speaker notes are its `notes` text, else the markdown slide's trailing notes comment; they are read one line per bullet or paragraph, split again after each sentence.
  req F-12.2:
    when: the `notes` setting is `subtitles` and a Presentation is presented
    then: the current slide's notes show over the bottom of the slide
  req F-12.3:
    when: the `notes` setting is `window` and a Presentation is presented
    then: a second window shows the current slide's notes, the time on the slide against its desired length, and the next slide's notes; it closes when the presentation ends
  req F-12.4: Arrow keys and Space pressed in the notes window move the deck as they do in the deck.
  req F-12.5: When the browser refuses the notes window, the deck shows a button that opens it.
  req F-12.6: A slide has an optional desired length (`duration`, seconds), edited with its other properties.
  req F-12.7: Other plugins add toolbar items and overlays through `PresenterSurface.Toolbar` and `PresenterSurface.Overlay`, and follow a presentation through `PresentationEventHandler`.
```

```mdl
feat F-13: Showcase Decks

  req F-13.1: A showcase's content can be one Slidev markdown deck: a summary slide first, then one slide per demo artifact, a video as a `backgroundVideo` slide and a screenshot as an image slide, with the demo's narration as that slide's notes.
  req F-13.2:
    when: CreateShowcase is invoked with content that F-6.7's rule splits into more than one slide
    then: the Presentation's first slides are the deck's parts in order, each an owned slide keeping its frontmatter and notes, followed by one linked slide per artifact, and each target gets a `Demonstrates` relation
  req F-13.3:
    when: CreateShowcase is invoked with content that is a single slide
    then: that content, unchanged, is the one owned slide before the artifact slides
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: Document presenter opens in fullscreen
  given: a Markdown document exists in the workspace
  when: user invokes TogglePresentation (keyboard or action menu)
  then:
    - the presenter companion fills the screen in the deck's fullscreen overlay
    - the Deck is visible with at least one slide
    - the URL is unchanged
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: Document slides split on separators
  given: a Markdown document with three `---`-separated sections
  when: DocumentArticle renders the document
  then:
    - three slides are produced
    - arrow-key navigation advances and retreats between slides
```

```mdl
scenario T-3: Exit returns to document view
  given: DocumentArticle is open in fullscreen
  when: user presses Escape
  then: the fullscreen overlay closes, leaving the document and its companion as they were
```

```mdl
scenario T-4: Presentation renders one slide per section
  given: a Presentation with one owned slide and one linked Markdown document
  when: PresentationArticle mounts
  then:
    - the grid shows two thumbnails, the owned slide first
    - the first thumbnail is selected
```

```mdl
scenario T-5: Slide advance
  given: PresentationArticle at slide 0 with a three-section Presentation
  when: user presses the right arrow
  then:
    - slide index advances to 1
    - the second thumbnail is selected
```

```mdl
scenario T-6: Slide index survives reload
  given: PresentationArticle at slide 1
  when: the app reloads and the Presentation is opened again
  then: slide 1 is shown
```

```mdl
scenario T-7: Keyboard shortcut registered
  given: a Markdown document node is focused in the app graph
  then:
    - action with key TogglePresentation is present on the node
    - keyBinding shows Shift+Cmd+P on macOS
```

```mdl
scenario T-8: Presentation presents fullscreen on its own plank
  given: a Presentation is open
  when: user presses `f`
  then:
    - the deck fills the screen with the overlay pager
    - Escape returns the deck to its plank
```

```mdl
scenario T-9: Reorder in the navtree
  given: a Presentation with three slides
  when: user drags the third slide to the top
  then: the deck order and the pager follow the navtree order
```

```mdl
scenario T-10: Removing a linked section keeps the object
  given: a Presentation with a linked Markdown document
  when: user removes the section
  then:
    - the section leaves the Presentation
    - the document still exists
```

---

## QA

Executable tests. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by test and step number.

```mdl
test QA-4: Slidev subset and click steps
  desc: Preview a document that uses layouts, click steps, a video background and an embedded surface, then step through it.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-6.1, F-6.2, F-6.3, F-7.1, F-7.2, F-7.3, F-7.4, F-8.1, F-8.2, F-8.3, F-9.1]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - plugin-markdown, plugin-presenter enabled
  steps:
    - name: Write the slides
      do: Create a document with a `two-cols` slide containing `::right::` and `<Surface ref="echo:///<id of another document>" />`, followed by a slide with `<v-clicks>` over a three-item list, and a slide with an unknown `layout`.
      expect: the Presenter companion shows the two-cols slide with the other document embedded on the right
    - name: Step clicks
      do: Open the list slide and press right three times, then once more.
      expect: each press reveals one item, the fourth moves to the next slide, and left from there lands on the list slide fully revealed
    - name: Unknown layout
      do: Go to the slide with the unknown layout.
      expect: it renders as a default slide without an error
    - name: Missing surface
      do: Change the embedded ref to `echo:///not-an-id`.
      expect: a "Missing object" placeholder shows, with no spinner
    - name: Print preview
      do: Click the deck, then open the browser's print preview.
      expect: one landscape page per slide of the deck, every list item visible and no toolbar or status bar
      note: The print container mounts at `beforeprint`, so content that loads asynchronously (Prism grammars, embedded surfaces, images) can be missing or blank in the printout; a print/export operation that awaits the container is a follow-up.

```

```mdl
test QA-1: Preview a document in the companion, then present it
  desc: The core presenter round-trip — create a document with slide separators, preview it in the presenter companion, present it fullscreen, then exit.
  actors: both
  covers: [F-1.1, F-1.2, F-2.1, F-2.2, F-2.3, T-1, T-3]
  status: unverified
  automated:
    - composer-e2e:presenter.spec.ts#Presenter › preview a document in the companion, then present it
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - collection: a collection in that space, to create into
    - plugin-presenter is enabled — it is OFF by default (absent from `getDefaults` in
      `plugin-defs.tsx`), though the plugin itself is registered unconditionally so it always
      appears in the plugin registry to enable manually
    - no document named "QA Slides" exists — ABORT rather than deleting one this test did not create
  steps:
    - name: Create a document with slides
      do: In the navtree, click + on a collection and choose Markdown. Name it "QA Slides".
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.markdown.createDraft { name: "QA Slides", content: "# Slide one\n\n---\n\n# Slide two\n" }
      capture: created
      expect: a Document named "QA Slides" now exists with two `---`-separated sections
      assert: return !!$created.object
    - name: Place it
      do: (the navtree create action places it for you)
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.addObject { object: $created.object, target: $given.collection }
      expect: "QA Slides" appears as a row under the collection
    - name: Preview in the companion
      do: Open "QA Slides", open its companion and pick the Presenter tab.
      expect: the companion shows "Slide one" as a slide scaled to the companion's width
    - name: Enter presentation mode
      do: Choose Present from the document's actions menu, or press Shift+Cmd+P (macOS) / Shift+Alt+P (Windows/Linux).
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.presenter.setPresenting { object: $created.object, state: true }
      expect: the slides fill the screen showing "Slide one", with no companion tab strip; the URL is unchanged
      assert: return document.body.innerText.includes('Slide one');
    - name: Exit presentation mode
      do: Press Escape.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.presenter.setPresenting { object: $created.object, state: false }
      expect: the document plank and its presenter companion are back as they were, and the URL is unchanged
      assert: return !!document.querySelector('[data-testid="deck.viewport"]');
  after:
    - name: Delete the document
      do: Right-click "QA Slides" in the navtree and choose Delete.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [$created.object], target: $given.collection }
      expect: the row leaves the navtree and its plank closes
```

```mdl
test QA-2: Showcase clip
  desc: |
    The 10s showcase clip: Present a document as slides and page through them. Recorded light at 60 fps with no ident, captions or
    count-in by `tools/autocue/showcase/overnight.mjs`; the clip is the `clip: presenter` step.
  actors: human
  status: unverified        # driven by autocue/showcase.mjs
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - plugin-markdown, plugin-presenter enabled
  steps:
    - name: Present a document
      do: Write a document split by --- and press Shift+Cmd+P.
      expect: the first slide fills the plank
    - name: Page through
      do: Press the right arrow three times.
      expect: each slide shows in turn
```

```mdl
test QA-3: Build and present a Presentation
  desc: Create a Presentation, add a slide, link a markdown document, reorder in the navtree, present it fullscreen, step, exit and reload.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-3.1, F-3.2, F-3.4, F-3.5, F-3.6, F-3.7, F-4.1, F-4.4, F-4.5, F-4.6, F-4.7, F-4.8, F-4.9, F-5.1, F-5.2, F-5.3, F-5.5, T-4, T-5, T-6, T-8, T-9, T-10]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - plugin-markdown, plugin-presenter enabled
  steps:
    - name: Create a Presentation
      do: In the space's create-object menu choose Presentation and name it "QA Deck".
      expect: "QA Deck" appears in the navtree as a folder with no children
    - name: Add a slide
      do: Open "QA Deck" and click the add-slide button.
      expect: a child "New slide" appears and the pager shows "1 / 1"
    - name: Link a document
      do: Use the link-object picker to link an existing markdown document.
      expect: the document appears as a second child and the pager shows "1 / 2"
    - name: Reorder
      do: Drag the second child above the first in the navtree.
      expect: the order of the children and of the deck follows the drag
    - name: Present
      do: Press `f`, then step with the arrow keys.
      expect: the deck fills the screen, the overlay pager shows and hides with pointer movement, and each arrow press changes the slide
    - name: Exit and reload
      do: Press Escape, then reload the app and reopen "QA Deck".
      expect: the deck is inline again and shows the slide that was current before the reload
    - name: Remove the linked document
      do: In the navtree, open the linked document's menu under "QA Deck" and choose "Remove from presentation".
      expect: the child leaves the folder, the pager shows "1 / 1", and the document is still in Collections
    - name: Delete the owned slide
      do: Open the owned slide's menu under "QA Deck"; it has no "Remove from presentation". Choose Delete.
      expect: the child leaves the folder and the pager shows "0 / 0"; undo brings the slide back
```

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: A dedicated `Presentation` object owns an ordered list of sections, each an owned markdown `Text` or a link to any object, and is shown in the navtree as a folder of slides.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Presentation, F-3, F-5]
  source: docs/DESIGN.md Q1
```

```mdl
decision D-2: One section is exactly one slide.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-3.2]
  source: docs/DESIGN.md Q2
```

```mdl
decision D-3: The markdown document companion stays as a quick preview split on `---`.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [DocumentArticle, F-2]
  source: docs/DESIGN.md Q2b
```

```mdl
decision D-4: An object without a slide surface still renders through a fallback chain ending in a title slide; the picker toggle filters to objects with a dedicated slide surface.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [SlideRenderer, F-4.9]
  source: docs/DESIGN.md Q3
```

```mdl
decision D-5: The current slide index is per-user, per-deck view state in `react-ui-attention` with the local backend.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [SlideViewState, F-4.7]
  source: docs/DESIGN.md Q4
```

```mdl
decision D-6: The pager is a separate `Pager` primitive; `Carousel` shares its styles.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Deck]
  source: docs/DESIGN.md Q5
```

```mdl
decision D-7: The assistant skill is annotated on `Presentation` only and `agentCanEnable`.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Presentation]
  source: docs/DESIGN.md Q6
```

```mdl
decision D-8: A presenter view is deferred to a later phase; speaker notes are parsed now.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Deck]
  source: docs/DESIGN.md Q7
```

```mdl
decision D-9: Slide syntax is a strict Slidev-compatible subset rendered by the plugin's own pipeline.
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-2]
  source: docs/DESIGN.md Q8
```

```mdl
decision D-10: Collection decks, the `presentCollections` setting and the Settings module are removed; a Presentation replaces them. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [Presentation, F-1, F-3]
  why: A first-class deck object makes the experimental collection mode redundant.
  rejected: Keeping collection decks behind the setting.
```

```mdl
decision D-11: Owned slides are parented to the presentation explicitly when created, not by a schema annotation. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [Presentation, F-3.8]
  why: A parent annotation would also adopt linked parentless objects, so deleting a Presentation could delete them.
  rejected: `Annotation.SetParent` on `sections`.
```

```mdl
decision D-12: A Presentation presents fullscreen on its own plank. Fills in [D-4].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [TogglePresentation, F-1.4, T-8]
  why: A Presentation has no presenter companion; its article is the deck.
  rejected: Giving Presentation a presenter companion.
```

```mdl
decision D-13: Fullscreen state is read per object, so a fullscreen change for one deck does not remount or refocus another. Fills in [D-12].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [PresentationArticle, DocumentArticle]
  why: The global layout mode changes for every deck when any one toggles.
  rejected: Reading the global layout mode.
```

```mdl
decision D-14: Clicking a slide child in the navtree opens that slide's own article, the markdown editor for an owned slide. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-5.4, SlideEditorArticle]
  why: Slides need an editing surface, and the navtree is where a slide is selected.
  rejected: Opening the presentation at that slide.
```

```mdl
decision D-15: An owned slide's navtree label is its name, else its first heading, else "Slide N". Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-5.2]
  why: The Text type carries a name field that a person sets deliberately, so it takes precedence.
```

```mdl
decision D-16: Removing an owned slide from the navtree is labelled "Remove from presentation". Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-5.5]
  why: The generic label "Remove from collection" misdescribes a delete of the owned Text.
```

```mdl
decision D-17: An owned slide has no navtree remove action; the space's undoable Delete is the only way to delete it, and a linked section keeps "Remove from presentation", which only unlinks. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  supersedes: D-16
  affects: [Presentation, F-3.6, F-5.5]
  why: A container remove that deletes cannot be undone, and an owned slide would show both remove and Delete.
  rejected: Routing an owned remove through the space delete operation under a "Delete slide" label.
```

```mdl
decision D-18: A section whose target was deleted is omitted from the deck and from the navtree folder; a target that has not loaded stays a pending slide. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [SlideSource, F-4.10, F-5.6]
  why: A deleted target never loads, so a pending placeholder would wait forever, and the pager and navtree must agree.
  rejected: A placeholder slide for a deleted target.
```

```mdl
decision D-19: A Presentation is tagged as a collection item, so it is filed into the space's Collections when created. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [Presentation, F-3.1]
  why: Without the tag a new Presentation is filed nowhere and cannot be found in the navtree.
```

```mdl
decision D-20: The Phase 1 fixes are applied in one wave after the running-app verification. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [Presentation]
  why: Bugs found in the running app then land with the review fixes in one set of commits.
```

```mdl
decision D-21: Inline, the Deck pager sits centered in a status bar below the slide, not in the top toolbar. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Deck]
  why: The toolbar keeps the editing actions; navigation sits under the slide it controls.
```

```mdl
decision D-22: Reveal.js and RevealPlayer are deleted; the document preview renders on the shared Deck with no setting. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [DocumentArticle, F-2]
  why: One renderer for decks and previews; the Settings module is gone, so there is nothing to put reveal behind.
```

```mdl
decision D-23: Slides are written in a strict Slidev-compatible subset (layouts, slots, click steps, notes, static line highlights); anything outside it is not rendered. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [MarkdownSlide, SlideLayouts, F-6, F-7]
  source: docs/DESIGN.md Q8
```

```mdl
decision D-24: Frontmatter gains `backgroundVideo` (looping, muted, autoplaying), `backgroundOpacity` and `backgroundPosition` as DXOS extensions to the Slidev subset. Fills in [D-23].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [SlideBackground, F-8.1]
  source: docs/DESIGN.md section 6
```

```mdl
decision D-25: A slide embeds an object with `<Surface ref="echo:///<id>" role="slide|section|card" />`, resolved through the same fallback chain as a linked section. Fills in [D-4].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [EmbeddedSurface, F-8.2, F-8.3]
  source: docs/DESIGN.md section 6
```

```mdl
decision D-26: No `@slidev/parser`; the slide splitter and frontmatter reader are owned in `src/markdown`. Fills in [D-23].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [MarkdownSlide, F-6.7]
  why: The parser is not in the repo and targets Node, while the splitter is about sixty lines and must run in the browser.
  rejected: Adding `@slidev/parser` as a dependency.
```

```mdl
decision D-27: Going back with left lands on the previous slide fully revealed, as Slidev does. Fills in [D-23].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [Deck, F-7.3]
  why: Returning to a slide to review it should show everything that was on it.
  rejected: Restarting the previous slide at step 0.
```

```mdl
decision D-28: Click steps are ephemeral and reset on slide change; only the slide index is view state. Fills in [D-5].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [Deck, F-7.4]
  why: A step count persisted across reloads would reopen a slide half-revealed with no cue why.
```

```mdl
decision D-29: Code blocks render with `SyntaxHighlighter` from `@dxos/react-ui-syntax-highlighter`, whose styles are inline, and the global highlight.js stylesheets are dropped. Fills in [D-22].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [MarkdownSlide, F-6.6]
  why: One highlighter across Composer, with no global CSS that leaks into the host app.
  rejected: Keeping highlight.js with its stylesheets.
```

```mdl
decision D-30: Embedded surfaces are rendered with the database of the slide's owner: an owned slide uses its Text's database and a preview slide the document's. Fills in [D-25].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [SlideRenderer, EmbeddedSurface, F-8.2]
  why: A ref to an object in the same space has to resolve without the slide naming the space.
  rejected: Threading the database through Deck for every slide source.
```

```mdl
decision D-31: A `---` / blank line / `key: value` / `---` block at the head of a slide reads as frontmatter, so a formatter that inserts a blank line does not lose it. Fills in [D-23].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [MarkdownSlide, F-6.7]
  why: A formatter-touched document would otherwise silently drop its layout and background.
  rejected: Excluding the decks from the formatter, which protects only those files.
```

```mdl
decision D-32: Printing is scoped to the focused or fullscreen deck: it sets `data-printing-deck` on `<html>` between `beforeprint` and `afterprint`, renders every slide into a print-only container, and every print rule is keyed on that attribute. Fills in [D-23].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [Deck, F-9.1, F-9.2]
  why: Unscoped print rules blank every other print in the app and overlap when two decks are open, and printing only the current slide drops the rest of the deck.
  rejected: A global `@media print` stylesheet that hides everything outside the deck.
```

```mdl
decision D-33: Print does not wait for asynchronous slide content; the limitation is recorded in QA-4 and a print/export operation that pre-mounts and awaits the print container is a follow-up. Fills in [D-32].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [Deck, F-9.1]
  why: The browser takes the print layout straight after `beforeprint`, which leaves no time for code grammars, embedded surfaces or images to load.
  rejected: Delaying `beforeprint`, which the browser does not allow.
```

```mdl
decision D-34: The theme scrim applies only in the `image` layout, over its full-bleed picture. Fills in [D-24].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [SlideBackground]
  why: Other layouts place text beside or away from the picture, and a scrim there would dim a `background` the author chose.
  rejected: A scrim over every image background.
```

```mdl
decision D-35: The frontmatter `title` is parsed and reserved; it is not rendered on the slide. Fills in [D-23].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [MarkdownSlide, F-6.1]
  why: Slidev uses it for the browser title and slide index, which have no presenter surface yet, and keeping it parsed avoids an unknown-key issue on converted decks.
```

```mdl
decision D-36: An embedded `<Surface ref>` whose target is a `Text` renders the text as a slide, not through the surface chain. Fills in [D-25].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [EmbeddedSurface, F-8.2]
  why: A `Text`'s section surface is a markdown editor, so embedding another deck's owned slide showed a tiny editor instead of the slide.
  rejected: Registering a slide surface for every `Text`, which would also change linked sections elsewhere.
```

```mdl
decision D-37: A link whose URL is removed as unsafe renders without `href` or a new-tab target. Fills in [D-23].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [MarkdownSlide]
  why: An empty `href` with `target="_blank"` opens the app itself in a new tab.
```

```mdl
decision D-38: An embed whose target already encloses it (the slide's subject or an embedding ancestor), or one nested more than 3 levels deep, renders an "Embedded in itself" placeholder. Fills in [D-25].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [EmbeddedSurface, F-8.2]
  why: An author-controlled document must not hang the app; a document that embeds itself, or two that embed each other, otherwise render without limit.
  rejected: Dropping `renderSurface` below the first embed, which would leave every nested surface a placeholder.
```

```mdl
decision D-39: Slides are themed through `--slide-*` CSS variables, with built-in `default`, `light`, `dark` and `serif` themes chosen by `theme:` headmatter or the Presentation's `theme` setting, which also carries color and font overrides. Fills in [D-23].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Presentation, MarkdownSlide, Deck, F-6.8, F-6.9]
  source: chat 2026-10-22 (themes Q1 option 2, Q2 option 1)
```

```mdl
decision D-40: Only the first slide's `theme:` is read, as Slidev headmatter, and the Presentation's `theme` name wins over it. Fills in [D-39].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [Deck, F-6.8, F-6.9]
  why: A per-slide theme would break the strict Slidev subset, and the object setting is the one a user edits in a form.
```

```mdl
decision D-41: Theme overrides accept only plain colors (hex, names, `rgb`/`hsl`/`oklch`-style functions of numbers) and font lists, checked in the schema and again at render. Fills in [D-39].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [SlideTheme, F-6.10]
  why: Override values reach inline styles from synced, author-controlled data; `url(...)` would load remote resources and a `;` could inject declarations.
```

```mdl
decision D-42: `light` and `dark` force their mode by setting `color-scheme` on the slide (the app tokens use `light-dark()`), and the code block passes the mode to `SyntaxHighlighter`'s new `themeMode` prop. Fills in [D-39].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [MarkdownSlide, F-6.8]
  why: The highlighter picks its palette in script from the app's mode, which CSS cannot override.
  rejected: Toggling the `.dark` class on the slide, which cannot switch a dark app's slide to light.
```

```mdl
decision D-43: An image whose URL is an object URI (`![label](echo:///<id>)`) embeds the object like `<Surface ref>` with the `slide` role; alone in its paragraph it fills its slot, and the label is ignored. Fills in [D-25].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [MarkdownSlide, F-8.2, F-8.4]
  why: Main's reveal player gained this syntax (#14152) and plugin-debug's presenter sample uses it to show a timeline chart; deleting reveal must not drop it.
```

```mdl
decision D-44: The slide editor previews the slide either below the editor in a vertical split or in the plank's companion; there is no picture-in-picture mode.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [SlideEditorArticle, F-10.3]
  source: chat 2026-10-23 (slide editor Q1 option 2, renderer at the bottom)
```

```mdl
decision D-45: The slide editor toolbar carries formatting, slide tools (layout, click step, column break, object, background, notes) and view controls.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [SlideEditorArticle, F-10.1, F-10.2]
  source: chat 2026-10-23 (slide editor Q2 option 1)
```

```mdl
decision D-46: The new slide editor serves Presentation slides only; markdown documents keep plugin-markdown's editor and the companion deck preview.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [SlideEditorArticle, DocumentArticle]
  source: chat 2026-10-23 (slide editor Q3 option 1)
```

```mdl
decision D-47: Cursor and preview sync both ways: the cursor's click group sets the preview step and outlines its slot, and clicking the preview selects the element's source through `data-source` ranges kept from mdast positions.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [SlideEditorArticle, MarkdownSlide, F-10.4, F-10.5]
  source: chat 2026-10-23 (slide editor Q4 option 2)
```

```mdl
decision D-48: Clicking the preview moves the editor's caret to the start of the element's source rather than selecting the source. Fills in [D-47].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [SlideEditorArticle, F-10.5]
  why: A selected range is replaced by the next keystroke, which a click meant only to navigate should not risk.
  source: chat 2026-10-23
```

```mdl
decision D-49: Each slide-toolbar action is one editor change, so one undo reverts it. Fills in [D-45].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [SlideEditorArticle, F-10.2]
  why: A toolbar action is one intent; an author undoing a layout pick or an inserted click group expects it gone in one step.
  rejected: Writing the slide's `content` through ECHO directly, which bypasses the editor's history and moves the cursor.
```

```mdl
decision D-50: Frontmatter edits go through the YAML document API, keeping the block's other keys, their order and its comments; malformed or non-mapping frontmatter is left as written. Fills in [D-45].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [SlideEditorArticle, F-10.2]
  why: The frontmatter is hand-written text; a picker must not reformat what the author wrote around the one key it sets.
  rejected: Re-serialising the parsed frontmatter object, which drops comments and reorders keys.
```

```mdl
decision D-51: A Presentation's article shows its slides as a grid of thumbnails without a pager; dragging a thumbnail reorders the sections and double-clicking presents from it. Supersedes the inline single-slide deck of [F-4.1].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [PresentationArticle, Deck, F-4.11, F-4.12, F-4.13]
  why: The article is where a deck is arranged; one slide at a time hides the order, and the slide editor already edits a single slide.
  rejected: A toggle between grid and single slide inline; presenting already shows one slide at a time.
```

```mdl
decision D-52: A theme's fonts are picked by name, a text font and a code font, from a fixed set; web fonts among them (Inter, Nunito, Source Serif 4, Fira Code, IBM Plex Mono) are imported only when a deck uses them. Supersedes the free-text font list of [F-6.9].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [SlideTheme, F-6.9]
  why: A picker is easier than writing a CSS font list, and a deck pays only for the fonts it picks.
  rejected: A free-text font-family list, which names fonts the app may not have; system font lists only, which look different on every machine.
```

```mdl
decision D-53: Two layouts beyond Slidev's set: `three-cols` (default content, then `::middle::` and `::right::`) and `grid`, 2 × 2 in reading order (default content, `::right::`, `::bottom-left::`, `::bottom-right::`); both, like `two-cols`, take `::left::` content into their first region, and "Start the next column" inserts the marker after the one holding the caret.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-6.1, MarkdownSlide, SlideToolbar]
  why: The user asked for a three-column and a 2 × 2 layout; reusing `::right::` keeps a two-cols slide valid when its layout is switched to either.
  rejected: Positional names such as `::top-left::` for the grid, which would make a two-cols slide lose its right column when switched to `grid`.
```

```mdl
decision D-54: A column bleeds to the slide's edges by a per-slide frontmatter key, `bleed: left | right`, rather than by an attribute on an embed; with it the layout pads its columns instead of its frame.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-8.5, MarkdownSlide]
  why: The user asked to optionally drop the padding around an embedded object; a column is the unit the padding belongs to, and frontmatter is where a slide's layout is already set.
  rejected: `<Surface … bleed />`, which would need negative margins matched to each layout's padding.
```

```mdl
decision D-55: Slides offer a three-column layout and a 2 × 2 layout. [D-53] records how they were filled in.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-6.1, F-6.2]
  why: Content often splits three ways or into a grid of four, which two columns cannot hold.
```

```mdl
decision D-56: A slide can drop the padding around an embedded object, so the object reaches the slide's edges. [D-54] records how it was filled in.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-8.5]
  why: An embedded object (a drawing, a map, an image) reads better edge to edge than inset in a padded column.
```

```mdl
decision D-57: The 2 × 2 layout is named `two-by-two`, not `grid`. Supersedes the name in [D-53].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-6.1, F-6.2, SlideLayouts]
  why: It matches the name dxos/dxos#14188 gives the same layout, and `grid` already names the presentation's thumbnail view.
```

```mdl
decision D-58: The deck and the slide are Radix-style composites, `Deck.*` and `Slide.*`, with a headless `Root`; they stay internal to the plugin until they move to a `react-ui-presenter` package.
  date: 2026-10-24
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Deck, Slide]
  why: Containers compose the parts they need (a grid inline, one slide fullscreen, a pager or not) instead of switching modes through props.
```

```mdl
decision D-59: `Deck.Root` holds the slides, index, click step, fullscreen and the key handler; `Deck.Content` is the focus scope (keys, print); the parent chooses `Deck.Viewport` or `Deck.Grid`, and the fullscreen pager lives inside `Deck.Viewport`. `Slide.Frame` needs no `Slide.Root`, so a bare markdown slide can be framed directly. Fills in [D-58].
  date: 2026-10-24
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [Deck, Slide]
  why: Fullscreen changes which parts render, so the parent that composes them decides; keeping the pager inside the viewport keeps it over the slide it pages.
  rejected: A `Deck.Overlay` part, which every fullscreen composition would have to remember to include.
```

```mdl
decision D-60: The text fonts add Space Grotesk, Mali, Geist, Orbitron, Unbounded and OpenDyslexic, each loaded on demand like the others of [D-52].
  date: 2026-10-24
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [SlideTheme, F-6.9]
  why: A wider choice of faces for decks, including OpenDyslexic for readability.
```

```mdl
decision D-61: LXGW WenKai joins the text fonts, loaded on demand and kept out of the web app's install-time cache, despite shipping as one 8.4 MB file per weight.
  date: 2026-10-24
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [SlideTheme, F-6.9]
  why: It covers Chinese text, which none of the other fonts do; on the web its size is paid only by decks that use it.
```

```mdl
decision D-62: Add two layouts beyond Slidev's built-ins: three-cols (slots `default`, `::middle::`, `::right::`) and two-by-two (`default`, `::right::`, `::bottom-left::`, `::bottom-right::`); "Start next column" inserts the marker of the column after the cursor's. Recorded on dxos/dxos#14188 as D-53; renumbered when merged, and [D-55] records the same request.
  date: 2026-10-24
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-6.2]
  why: Comparison and quadrant slides need more than two columns.
```

```mdl
decision D-63: In the presentation grid, double-clicking a slide or adding one opens it in the slide editor; the toolbar's add button is a split button whose caret sets the layout later adds use; a ghost tile after the last slide adds one; a tile's context menu hides or shows a slide and deletes it; the toolbar presents with the editor's present icon and has no fullscreen button; a slide can be hidden from the presentation.
  date: 2026-10-24
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [PresentationArticle, Deck, SlideGrid]
  why: The grid is where a deck is assembled, so opening, adding, hiding and removing slides belong there; presenting is the one way to go fullscreen.
```

```mdl
decision D-64: A slide is hidden by Slidev's own frontmatter key, `hide: true`; presenting skips it while the grid still shows it, dimmed with an eye-slash, and the presented index maps back to the slide's position in the whole deck. Deleting an owned slide invokes the space's undoable `RemoveObjects`, as the navtree does; a linked object is only unlinked. Fills in [D-63].
  date: 2026-10-24
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-6.1, PresentationArticle, SlideGrid]
  why: Keeping to Slidev's key keeps a deck portable; the stored index stays the grid's, so hiding a slide never moves the viewer's place.
  rejected: A `hidden` flag on the section ref, which a linked object could carry but plain markdown could not.
```

```mdl
decision D-65: A grid tile's right-click menu is the app's context menu for the slide's graph node, not a menu of the grid's own: it lists the node's navtree actions (delete, remove from presentation), and hiding or showing a slide is a graph action on owned slides. Supersedes the grid-local menu of [D-63].
  date: 2026-10-24
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [PresentationArticle, SlideGrid]
  why: One context menu for the whole app, whose items plugins contribute by context, rather than a menu per component.
```

```mdl
decision D-66: A Presentation holds `Slide` objects rather than bare section refs; a Slide refs its content (an owned Text or a linked object) and carries the slide's own metadata. A Presentation gains a description, and `sections` is renamed `slides`.
  date: 2026-10-24
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Presentation, Slide, F-11.1, F-11.2]
  why: A section was always exactly one slide, and metadata that applies to any slide (hidden, notes, an image) had nowhere to live for a linked object.
```

```mdl
decision D-67: Slide metadata that applies to any content (`hidden`, `notes`, `image`, `title`) lives on the `Slide`; `layout` and `background` stay in a markdown slide's frontmatter, and an export writes the fields back as frontmatter.
  date: 2026-10-24
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Slide, F-11.1]
  why: A linked object has no frontmatter, so frontmatter alone could not hide or annotate it.
  rejected: Keeping everything in frontmatter, which is portable Slidev but serves owned markdown slides only.
```

```mdl
decision D-68: A slide's image is a ref to a plugin-studio `MediaArtifact`, which the slide background resolves; it is generated through plugin-studio's `StudioOperation.Generate`, not a provider called directly.
  date: 2026-10-24
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Slide, GenerateSlideImage, F-11.4, F-11.5]
  why: The artifact keeps the image's provenance and variants, and studio owns provider choice.
  rejected: Writing the image URL into frontmatter `image:`, which renders today but loses the link to the artifact.
```

```mdl
decision D-69: The prototype is a story of a slide beside the assistant companion, with a mocked AI service whose scripted reply calls the real `GenerateSlideImage` tool, which writes the image onto the slide. Fills in [D-66] and [D-68].
  date: 2026-10-24
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-11.3, F-11.4]
  why: It shows the slide-scoped assistant end to end without a network, with only the model's reply scripted.
```

```mdl
decision D-70: plugin-presenter displays speaker notes while presenting; a plugin setting chooses a separate window or subtitles over the presented slide. Each slide has a field for its desired length. Supersedes the deferral of [D-8].
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: user:richburdon
  supersedes: D-8
  affects: [PresenterSettings, Slide, F-12]
```

```mdl
decision D-71: The plugin has a Settings module again, holding only the `notes` setting. Fills in [D-70].
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  supersedes: D-10
  affects: [PresenterSettings]
  why: [D-70] asks for a plugin setting; [D-10] removed the module along with the collection-deck setting it held.
```

```mdl
decision D-72: The notes window is a React portal into `window.open`, carrying the app's stylesheets and theme, with the deck's keys forwarded from it; subtitles are fixed white on black like video captions. Fills in [D-70].
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [PresentedOverlay, SpeakerNotes, F-12.3, F-12.4]
  why: A portal keeps one React tree, so the notes follow the deck's state with no messaging between windows.
  rejected: A separate route opened in the window, which would need its own client and a channel to the deck.
```

```mdl
decision D-73: Presenter offers `PresenterSurface.Toolbar`, `PresenterSurface.Overlay` and the `PresentationEventHandler` capability, so plugin-recorder can add a Record item, draw its indicator over the deck and follow the slides without presenter depending on it. Fills in [D-70].
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-12.7, PresentedOverlay]
  why: The recorder needs the deck's slide changes and a place in its toolbar; the dependency must point from recorder to presenter.
```

```mdl
decision D-74: `PresentationEventHandler.onStop` fires a task after the presented deck unmounts, and a remount for the same presentation cancels it. Fills in [D-73].
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [PresentedOverlay, F-12.7]
  why: React's StrictMode remounts at once in development, which otherwise stopped a recording the moment it started.
```

```mdl
decision D-75: A Slide has an array of takes (plugin-studio Variants, owned by the slide) and a main take, so each slide keeps its own voice-over recordings.
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Slide]
```

```mdl
decision D-76: A plugin-projects showcase is a Presentation: its write-up is the first slide and each artifact (an image or video, a diagram, a pull request) a linked slide after it, linked to the features it shows by `Demonstrates`.
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [Presentation, CreateShowcase]
```

```mdl
decision D-77: Presenter implements plugin-projects' `CreateShowcase` operation and migrates `Showcase` 0.1.0 into a Presentation in place, so the deck keeps the showcase's id and its `Demonstrates` edges. Fills in [D-76].
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [Presentation, CreateShowcase]
  why: Presenter already depends on plugin-projects through plugin-studio, so only this side can name both the deck and the relation.
```

```mdl
decision D-78: `CreateShowcase` accepts a whole deck as its content: a summary slide, then a slide per demo video (a `backgroundVideo` slide) or screenshot (an image slide), with the demo's narration as each slide's notes, split as the document preview splits it. Fills in [D-76].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [CreateShowcase, F-13.1, F-13.2, F-13.3]
  why: A pull request's showcase is written outside the app as one deck, and one operation keeps one path from that deck to a Presentation linked by `Demonstrates`; splitting it as the preview does keeps every slide's frontmatter and notes, which feed the teleprompter (F-12).
  rejected:
    - "A separate deck-import operation in presenter: a second way to make the same Presentation, without the `Demonstrates` edges."
```

---

## Appendix: Extension Definitions

Extension block types used in this document are defined below using
the core `ext` primitive — the only construct the base language provides.

```mdl
ext type
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0
  desc: A named data structure with typed fields and optional literals.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    fields?: FieldMap
    literals?: UnionList
    extends?: TypeRef[]
```

```mdl
ext feat
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0
  desc: A named feature grouping one or more requirements.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    req: RequirementList
  nesting: self
```

```mdl
ext scenario
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0
  desc: An acceptance scenario expressed as given / when / then steps.
  fields:
    given?: Step | Step[]
    when?: Step | Step[]
    then: Step | Step[]
    tags?: TagList
```

```mdl
ext component
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0
  desc: A UI component with props, internal state, slots, actions, and events.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    props?: FieldMap
    state?: FieldMap
    slots?: FieldMap
    actions?: ActionMap
    emits?: EventMap
    layout?: CodeBlock
```

```mdl
ext op
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.op@1.0
  desc: |
    A named operation with typed inputs, outputs, and declared errors.
    Pure ops have no effects or requires. Effectful ops declare both.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    input?: FieldMap
    output?: TypeExpr
    errors?: ErrorMap
    effects?: EffectList
    requires?: ServiceList
    note?: Prose
```
